{
  "$comment": [
    "One accountable per decision type and scope (V22). The change manager is accountable for tier 3 and emergency change authorization, with its own group for a tier 3 emergency. The change board is accountable for exceptions about a change (document 28, issues 2 and 4). The configuration admin is the one accountable for both configuration decision types (document 28, issue 6).",
    "Aligned with the process documents (document 21, B21-9): the builder does the work of a tier decision (P02), the platform admin does the work of an ownership hand-over (P08), and the sponsor's priority card falls back to the business owner, which for a request with no application is the person the intake names (P01 step 8). Flagged agents: the AI lead decides, the platform admin does the work, the business owner is consulted, and AI drafts the options (P06, P08)."
  ],
